WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.305
This one happens every week.

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.882
Start on the brand that's hosting

3
00:00:05.926 --> 00:00:07.815
switch to it from Home.

4
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.753
Then tap plus,

5
00:00:10.757 --> 00:00:12.013
Create event,

6
00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:14.222
and Ticketed event.

7
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.343
The basics are the same as any event.

8
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:22.396
Name it, and say how people attend.

9
00:00:23.137 --> 00:00:24.856
Pick a party type,

10
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.421
then the vibe tags

11
00:00:26.421 --> 00:00:27.988
and the genres you'll play.

12
00:00:29.171 --> 00:00:30.841
Add a short description,

13
00:00:30.841 --> 00:00:33.286
so guests know what a night looks like.

14
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.445
Step two is where it changes.

15
00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:47.472
Choose Recurring.

16
00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:49.701
Set the first date,

17
00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.411
then when doors open

18
00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:53.283
and when the night ends.

19
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.584
Now the pattern:

20
00:00:55.677 --> 00:00:57.823
weekly, on a Tuesday.

21
00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.971
A recurring event always needs an end,

22
00:01:02.003 --> 00:01:04.558
so choose when the run stops

23
00:01:04.694 --> 00:01:06.715
after a set number of nights,

24
00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:07.981
or on a date.

25
00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:11.511
The summary shows the whole schedule,

26
00:01:11.511 --> 00:01:12.966
in your timezone.

27
00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:18.917
Step three:

28
00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:20.020
where.

29
00:01:20.504 --> 00:01:23.610
Name the venue and search for the address.

30
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.313
With hide address on,

31
00:01:26.313 --> 00:01:28.333
only ticket holders see it.

32
00:01:30.913 --> 00:01:33.180
Step four is how it looks.

33
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.253
Add a video cover.

34
00:01:35.669 --> 00:01:38.132
Mingla uploads it and gets it ready

35
00:01:38.132 --> 00:01:39.811
we've sped that part up

36
00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:41.796
and the sheet updates

37
00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:43.385
on its own when it's done.

38
00:01:44.279 --> 00:01:46.479
Add more photos underneath,

39
00:01:46.508 --> 00:01:47.634
up to eight.

40
00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:49.989
Then the theme:

41
00:01:50.021 --> 00:01:52.275
a colour, a typeface,

42
00:01:52.293 --> 00:01:53.716
and a little motion.

43
00:01:54.085 --> 00:01:56.572
The preview changes as you choose.

44
00:02:17.747 --> 00:02:20.061
Step five: tickets.

45
00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:22.992
Name the ticket and describe it.

46
00:02:23.658 --> 00:02:25.069
Set the price

47
00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.707
dollars, for this brand

48
00:02:26.727 --> 00:02:28.707
and how many seats you have.

49
00:02:29.543 --> 00:02:31.479
Turn on a waitlist,

50
00:02:31.479 --> 00:02:34.070
and allow transfers so a guest

51
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.700
can pass a ticket on.

52
00:02:36.793 --> 00:02:39.189
Save it, and you'll see capacity

53
00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:40.753
and the most it can take.

54
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:46.174
In settings, keep it public.

55
00:02:46.545 --> 00:02:48.393
Selling at the door as well?

56
00:02:48.787 --> 00:02:51.207
Turn on in-person payments.

57
00:02:52.847 --> 00:02:54.787
Step seven checks demand

58
00:02:54.787 --> 00:02:56.353
for your next date.

59
00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:59.395
It's a likely range, not a promise.

60
00:02:59.811 --> 00:03:02.827
Publish, and sales open straight away.
